  "contracts": [
    "An eligible post-RTI interrupt reads the actual vector, backs SP by9 and applies masks without frame reads/writes or instruction retirement",
    "All SP/target values and old/saved CCR pairs match independent CPU/frame expectations; saved X bytes remain unchanged when restored X cannot rise",
    "Normal, waiting and returned frame modes have distinct warm same-vector entries in the bounded native cache",
    "Only a successfully completed RTI creates the boundary; the next retired instruction consumes it, another RTI replaces it, and CLI replaces it with actual IRQ deferral",
    "Ordinary retirement retains the existing zero-control check and adds no helper or new status branch; extra classification occurs only in its existing nonzero-control path",
    "The board can query interrupt_frame_available separately from source eligibility; active/fault boundaries cannot deliver a reused frame",
    "Checkpoints retain returned-frame status, fault metadata and deferral; invalid idle/deferral combinations fail before mutation",
    "Actual refused vector reads retain effects and exact diagnosis, latch against replay, and recovered entry rereads a changed real vector",
    "An authored fetched reset/WAI/two-handler/RTI program runs seven actual native instructions and resumes at the real following program instruction",
    "All23 actual consumers use the same strict optimized library and verified exec identities; no firmware or copied manufacturer program is embedded"
  ],
